vte: keep text readable (minimum contrast), on by default

Text whose WCAG 2 contrast ratio against its background is below the
minimum is drawn lighter or darker in draw_cells(), mixing it toward
white or black so that its hue stays.  Covers normal text, selection,
the character under the block cursor and input-method text; only the
drawing changes.  Text with the same color chosen for text and
background (hidden) is left alone; dim text gets half the margin.

The ratio is the new property VteTerminal:minimum-contrast (1.0 = off;
no new C functions), default 3.0 or VTE_MINIMUM_CONTRAST from the
environment.  Same as xterm's minimumContrast resource.

Apply after vte-0.84.1-do-not-use-std-out_ptr.patch.

Commits (branch min-contrast on vte-0.84.1):
  a8f6e31 Keep text readable: minimum contrast, on by default
  7a537c4 Add VteTerminal:minimum-contrast property

